@bank all
// SW4's words for TB3's milestone cards (0.99.5, TR1 item 2; MS995 in section 18's Traditions slot, behind TRAD995_ON).
// Keys milestone.<id>.open / mid / reply.N (your three lines) / answer.N (the host's reply to reply N) / close. One line
// each, so a reply always matches its answer. No placeholders: the card fills none.
// Calder: few words, numbers not adjectives, no "well done" (her story's payoff is Four weeks aboard). Zeke: quick and
// warm, never calls a job easy.

// new-hands-tea (host calder): your first Friday, the Works tea corner
== milestone.new-hands-tea.open
- Sit. The first Friday's tea belongs to the new hand. The rule's older than me.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.mid
- Five days. Nothing of yours has come back to the board. That's the number I watch.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.reply.1
- It's been a lot, Chief.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.answer.1
- It is. Week two's less. By week three it's just the work.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.reply.2
- I think I'm going to like it here.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.answer.2
- Hm. Say that again at four weeks. I'll remember you said it.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.reply.3
- (Drink your tea quietly)
== milestone.new-hands-tea.answer.3
- Good. Quiet's allowed at this table. Most days it's encouraged.
== milestone.new-hands-tea.close
- Your mug's on the rack now. That's where it lives. Fridays, this corner.

// six-weeks-aboard (host torres-zeke): a tea in the bow lounge
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.open
- Six weeks! Sit, sit. I've borrowed the good mugs from the bar. Nobody tell the bar.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.mid
- First morning, you asked me which way the Works was. Now Pell asks you where things are.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.reply.1
- I still get lost sometimes.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.answer.1
- Course you do. So do I. I'm fairly sure coil three moves at night.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.reply.2
- Thanks for showing me the ropes, Zeke.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.answer.2
- Cheers. You asked the right questions. Loads of them. That's half of it, honestly.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.reply.3
- So what comes next?
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.answer.3
- Bigger jobs. Longer rounds. One day, a new hand of your own to show round.
== milestone.six-weeks-aboard.close
- To six weeks. And the next six, done properly. Drink up before the bar notices.

// twelve-weeks-aboard (host calder): her toast in the mess
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.open
- Twelve weeks. A quarter of a year aboard. I checked the log.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.mid
- This isn't a speech. It's a cup of tea with more people standing near it.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.reply.1
- Thanks, Chief. For all of it.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.answer.1
- Don't. You did the jobs. I signed the cards. That's all it was.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.reply.2
- Here's to the next twelve.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.answer.2
- The next twelve. I'll want the numbers. I always want the numbers.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.reply.3
- (Raise your cup)
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.answer.3
- Hm. Cups up, all of you. Properly up.
== milestone.twelve-weeks-aboard.close
- To the hand who isn't new any more. Back to it tomorrow.
